00 square miles (3,103,200 square km).\'  But prior to Russian rule, the Sakha and other Siberian peoples employed a decentralized clan system. Furthermore, they were pastoralists. This makes the identification of a \'typical\' travel time between clans more difficult.'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2190, 'temperature': 0.2})
